> is there a way of selecting everything from a list without entering
> every letter? Let's say I wanted to check cursing status by dropping
> everything that's not known to be blessed or cursed, so I press D, X and
> then have to select 20 or more items. Or is there a way of just
> selecting everything from that list?

There are a bunch of commands for selecting parts of menus. The one I
use most often is '.', which selects every option on every page. (There
are also keys like ',' which selects every option on the current page,
and options to invert the selection or deselect the entire menu or the
page; I don't use those very often, so i don't know them offhand.)

The exact keys theoretically depend on the port, but tend to be
relatively consistent in practice. Look up the "menu_select_" options in
an options list, or perhaps in the Guidebook.

